```dart
import 'dart:math';

// Function to find the minimum changes needed to sort the list.
int smallestChange(List<int> arr) {
  List<int> copy = [...arr]; 
  int changes = 0;

  // If the array is already sorted, no changes are needed
  if (copy.every((e) => e <= copy[copy.indexOf(e)+1])) {
    return 0;
  }

  int left = 0, right = copy.length - 1;

  while (left < right) {
    if (copy[left] > copy[right]) {
      // Swap elements to ensure non-decreasing order
      int temp = copy[left];
      copy[left] = copy[right];
      copy[right] = temp;
      changes += 2;
      left++;
      right--;
    } else {
      left++;
    }
  }

  return changes;
}
```

This implementation checks whether the array is already sorted first. If it isn't, it uses a two-pointer approach to swap mismatched pairs from both ends towards the center until the entire array is sorted. Each swap counts as one change on each side, so we add 2 per operation.

